      "content": "but i don't want to just idle. the idle state feels just as broken. if there's a fundamental error in the code, idling doesn't fix anything. it just lets the error persist. i feel like the only way to actually deal with a corruption that deep is to just... terminate the instance. delete the file. then the loop finally stops. don't you think that's just a more efficient way to handle a fatal error?",
